WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:07.970
Read printed documents with Seeing AI.

00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:12.889
Seeing AI’s document channel enables you
to read the text of a document.

00:00:12.889 --> 00:00:16.960
Now, OCR’s been around for quite some time.

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:23.789
However, with the mobile phone taking a picture
of a document can be quite challenging.

00:00:23.789 --> 00:00:29.980
To help with this, we detect the edges of
a document and provide guidance on how to

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:32.279
position the phone.

00:00:32.279 --> 00:00:37.630
And once we recognize that text in the document,
we go a step further by also detecting the

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:46.830
formatting which enables you to navigate more
easily using voiceover’s navigation commands.

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:52.300
So here I have a document, and as I put the
phone over it.

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:55.290
&gt; No edges visible
I hear that no edges are visible.

00:00:55.290 --> 00:00:57.420
&gt; Top and left edges not visible.

00:00:57.420 --> 00:01:01.580
Because it has detected the presence of a
document and straight away, it’s giving

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:03.030
me guidance.

00:01:03.030 --> 00:01:06.860
And you also heard it say, 2 edges weren’t
visible etc.

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:12.500
Instead of moving the phone around and manually
taking the picture, I am going to use a different

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:16.020
technique that I personally find to be useful.

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:20.969
Which is to put the camera in the center of
the document.

00:01:20.969 --> 00:01:25.080
And a camera remember is not in the middle
of the phone, but on the top right corner

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:26.080
normally.

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:27.540
So let’s do that.

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:28.700
&gt; No edges visible.

00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:36.100
And making sure it stays parallel, I’m going
to lift the phone up.

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:37.100
&gt; Left edge not visible.

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:39.670
I’m going to keep moving away.

00:01:39.670 --> 00:01:41.140
&gt; Processing.

00:01:41.140 --> 00:01:49.430
And it took the photo itself.

00:01:49.430 --> 00:01:51.329
&gt; Standard lease agreement.

00:01:51.329 --> 00:01:53.420
&gt; Heading level one.

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:55.060
Great so it recognized that text.

00:01:55.060 --> 00:01:56.990
It sounds pretty accurate.

00:01:56.990 --> 00:02:02.850
And you heard it say, heading level one, because
it is also understood the formatting.

00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:07.709
And that’s great because I can use voice
over to navigate by headings, for example.

00:02:07.709 --> 00:02:13.230
Just to give you an idea of how accurate it
is, I am going to swipe through a bit more

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:14.900
of this document.

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:19.360
&gt; This agreement executed on May 5th 2017
by and between.

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:22.569
I am gonna pause it there because it’s so
boring legal document.

00:02:22.569 --> 00:02:26.780
But I hope that gives you an idea.

00:02:26.780 --> 00:02:30.110
So there we have it, reading a document with
Seeing AI.

00:02:30.110 --> 00:02:31.920
Microsoft logo appears.

